Appendix E: Navascués–Pironio–Acín (NPA) Hierarchy

E.1 Definition

For a given set of measurement operators, the NPA hierarchy constructs a sequence of outer approximations to \mathcal{C}_{\text{quant}} via semidefinite programming. At level k, one considers a moment matrix \Gamma indexed by words of length at most k in the measurement operators, subject to positivity, normalisation, and linear constraints encoding the given correlation tensor.

E.2 SDP Formulation

The feasibility problem at level k is:

\begin{aligned}
\text{find } &\Gamma\succeq0\\
\text{subject to } &\Gamma_{1,1}=1,\\
&\Gamma_{w,w'}=\overline{\Gamma_{w',w}},\\
&C_{i_1\dots i_n}=\Gamma_{e,w_{i_1\dots i_n}}.
\end{aligned}

E.3 Connection to Conjecture 4.5.3

Each communication round in a multi‑agent protocol allows the agents to correlate measurement choices, effectively lengthening the operator products appearing in the moment matrix. This suggests that the set \mathcal{L}_n(T) of correlations achievable in T rounds is contained in the T-th level NPA outer approximation, and that the limit T\to\infty recovers the full quantum set \mathcal{C}_{\text{quant}}.

